Note: =====================================================================
Note: hello_live.flow — Phase 38 LIVE-01 chapter
Note: =====================================================================
Note:
Note: The minimal `live <quantize> { ... }` block — a single 4-note melody
Note: that auto-loops at the next bar boundary. This is the smallest possible
Note: composer experience for the new Phase 38 live-coding surface.
Note:
Note: Run (one-shot smoke):
Note:   dotnet run --project flow-interpreter examples/live/hello_live.flow
Note:
Note: Run (live hot-swap mode):
Note:   dotnet run --project flow-interpreter -- --watch examples/live/hello_live.flow
Note:
Note:   While the watch is running, edit the `Sequence melody = | ... |`
Note:   line below and SAVE. The new content swaps in at the next bar
Note:   boundary with a 64-sample equal-power crossfade — no click, no
Note:   re-init of voices whose names survive the edit (LIVE-03 voice-pool
Note:   name-key preservation; D-38-06 micro-crossfade lock).
Note:
Note: Stderr advisory (D-v1.5-07):
Note:   On every entry into a `live { ... }` block, Flow emits a one-shot
Note:   stderr line `[live] entering live block at line N — opts OUT of
Note:   two-run cmp-clean determinism`. This is by design — live blocks
Note:   explicitly opt out of Phase 18/25/27/28/29/33/36/37 byte-identity
Note:   so the composer can edit mid-set without the determinism contract
Note:   surprising them. Offline render paths (writeWav / writeMidi)
Note:   STAY deterministic — the opt-out is scoped to live mode only.
Note:
Note: Quantize forms (per D-38-02):
Note:   live 1bar { ... }      Bar-quantized (default, also: 2bar, 4bar, ...)
Note:   live q { ... }         Quarter-note quantized
Note:   live h { ... }         Half-note quantized
Note:   live { ... }           Omitted quantize → 1-bar default

use "@std"
use "@audio"

tempo 120 {
    timesig 4/4 {
        key Cmajor {
            live 1bar {
                section main {
                    Sequence melody = | C4q D4q E4q F4q |
                }
                Song song = [main]
                Buffer result = (renderSong song "piano")
                (play result)
            }
        }
    }
}
